---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {connected} from '../lib/jobs';
---
<Layout title="Test the completed-job workflow"><section class="wrap section steps"><p class="eyebrow">Owner review</p><h1>One job.<br/>Added once.</h1><p class="callout">{connected?'Sanity is configured. These feeds show published CMS records from the latest build.':'Sanity account connection is still required. The site currently has no CMS records; the installation photograph is an existing brand asset.'}</p><ol><li>Open the job editor on your phone and choose <strong>Completed Jobs → New</strong>.</li><li>Select a city and service, enter the short job details, and add photos.</li><li>Save the draft and select <strong>Submit for review</strong>. Drafts stay out of website feeds.</li><li>The reviewer checks the photos and description, then selects <strong>Publish</strong>.</li><li>A successful website rebuild places the job on the matching service page and in the three most recently published jobs on the homepage.</li></ol><p>On Sanity Free, editing testers have Administrator access and can publish. “Submit for review” demonstrates the process; it does not enforce a separate approver. Formal draft-only permissions require a later plan decision.</p><h2>Older Wix jobs</h2><p>Imported jobs use the same fields plus their original Wix page URL and a stable import ID. Their photo list stays attached to the record. Unknown completion dates remain blank. An editorial feed date controls ordering, so importing old jobs does not push new jobs off the homepage.</p><div class="links"><a href="/">View homepage feed →</a><a href="/services/gas-tank-water-heaters/">View gas tank feed →</a></div></section></Layout>
